Coding Guidelines
1. Astro 5.x Core

Router: Use <ClientRouter /> from astro:transitions in the main Layout. DO NOT use <ViewTransitions />.

Prefetching: Add data-astro-prefetch to all primary navigation links (header, footer).

Images: ALWAYS use <Image /> from astro:assets with explicit width and height to avoid CLS.

Islands: Default to static. Use client:visible only for interactive UI parts. Avoid client:load unless required.

2. Layouts

Every page MUST use a Layout component.

No standalone pages without Layout.

No <html>, <head>, <body> outside Layouts.

3. Project Structure & Imports

Path Aliases: Use @/ for imports. No relative ../../ paths.

Components:

src/components/ui/ — buttons, inputs, primitives.

src/components/sections/ — hero, about, feature blocks.

Assets:

Use src/assets/ for images imported into components.

Use public/ only for static files (favicon, robots.txt).

4. TypeScript & Data Flow

Props: ALWAYS define interface Props in frontmatter.

interface Props {
  title: string;
  description?: string;
}
const { title, description } = Astro.props;

Guards: Use early returns (if (!data) return;).

Async (Server): Wrap external API calls in try/catch. Log meaningful errors.

Async (Client/Islands): Handle loading, error, and empty states in UI.

5. Styling (Tailwind CSS)

Utility-First: No @apply. Write utilities in markup.

Mobile-First: Base classes for mobile. Use md: / lg: for larger screens.

Dark Mode: ALWAYS include dark: variants for colors and backgrounds.

Global CSS: Only in src/styles/global.css. Avoid component-scoped CSS unless necessary.

6. Performance & Metrics
- Targets: Aim for First Contentful Paint < 1.8s, CLS < 0.1, and 60fps animations.
- Bundle: Keep client-side JS bundle < 200KB. Use dynamic imports for heavy interactions.
- Optimization:
  - Debounce/throttle user inputs (search, resize, scroll).
  - Use requestAnimationFrame for JS animations if CSS is not enough.
  - Avoid client-side JS unless required.
  - Keep Layout free of heavy JS.

7. Accessibility (A11y)

Use semantic HTML: <header>, <nav>, <main>, <section>, <article>, <footer>.

Interactive elements must have visible text or aria-label.

Never remove focus styles without providing focus-visible alternatives.

8. SEO

One <h1> per page.

Pass title and description to Layout.

Use meaningful alt text for images.

9. Data & Content (Astro Specific)
Content Collections: Use src/content/ and defineCollection for structured data (blog posts, projects, team members).

Type Safety: Use zod schemas in src/content/config.ts to validate data types strictly.

Fetch: Use getCollection() to retrieve data typesafely.

Git
Commits: Provide full command: git commit -m "feat: description".